  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agribusiness management course LUMS &#x2013; guest lectures</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lahore University of Management Sciences (LUMS) offers quite good quality Agribusiness Management courses, mainly aimed at Pakistani farm managers. This capacity building project further improves the quality and relevancy of these courses by providing guest lecturers on Dutch topics of excellence in the dairy and potato value chains during the courses in 2019 and 2020. In addition, a Training of Trainers (ToT) component is offered to Pakistani lecturers of LUMS to ensure that the contents of the guest lectures are integrated into future courses. A Dutch knowledge institute will perform the lectures and ToT training. This support is a continuation of earlier well-regarded support to LUMS in the form of scholarships and guest lectures, focusing on the dairy sector from 2015.</narrative>
  </description>
